<BaseLayout title="LI11 (Quchi) — Pool at the Crook Point" description="Learn how to locate and stimulate LI11 (Quchi) — the Pool at the Crook point. Benefits include allergy relief, skin health support, and immune system strengthening." breadcrumbs={[{ label: "Home", href: "/" }, { label: "Points", href: "/points" }, { label: "LI11 (Quchi)", href: "/points/li11-quchi-acupressure-point" }]} datePublished="2025-03-20" dateModified="2026-05-15" articleSchema={true}>
  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-12 lg:px-6">
    <h1 class="mb-4">LI11 (Quchi) — Pool at the Crook</h1>
    <p class="text-stone-500 dark:text-stone-400 text-lg mb-8">LI11, known as Quchi or Pool at the Crook, is a key point for clearing heat, treating allergies, skin conditions, and supporting immune function.</p>

    <section class="mb-8"><h2 class="mb-4">Location</h2>
    <img src="/images/li11-location.webp" alt="LI11 acupressure point location at the outer elbow" class="w-full max-w-sm mx-auto rounded-xl shadow-sm" />
    <p class="mb-3">LI11 is at the outer end of the elbow crease, in the depression that forms when the elbow is bent. It lies midway between the lateral epicondyle of the humerus and the elbow crease.</p>

    </section><section class="mb-8"><h2 class="mb-4">Benefits &amp; Uses</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-3 space-y-1 text-stone-700 dark:text-stone-300">
      <li><strong>Allergies:</strong> LI11 helps relieve hay fever, allergic rhinitis, sinus congestion, and hives.</li>
      <li><strong>Skin health:</strong> It is used for eczema, psoriasis, acne, and other inflammatory skin conditions.</li>
      <li><strong>Immune support:</strong> LI11 strengthens the immune system and helps the body fight infections.</li>
      <li><strong>Fever and inflammation:</strong> It clears heat from the body and helps reduce fever and inflammation.</li>
      <li><strong>Elbow and arm pain:</strong> LI11 can relieve tennis elbow, elbow stiffness, and arm fatigue.</li>
    </ul>

    </section><section class="mb-8"><h2 class="mb-4">How to Massage LI11</h2>
    <ol class="list-decimal pl-6 space-y-2 text-stone-700 dark:text-stone-300">
      <li>Bend your elbow to expose the outer elbow crease.</li>
      <li>Place your opposite thumb on the LI11 point at the end of the crease.</li>
      <li>Apply firm pressure with a small circular or pumping motion.</li>
      <li>Hold for 30?0 seconds, then switch arms.</li>
      <li>Repeat 2— times daily during allergy season.</li>
    </ol>

    </section><section class="mb-8"><h2 class="mb-4">Science &amp; Research</h2>
    <p class="mb-3">A 2018 systematic review in <em>Annals of Allergy, Asthma &amp; Immunology</em> found that LI11 acupuncture (and acupressure) significantly reduced symptoms of allergic rhinitis compared to sham treatment.<sup><a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/29337636/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">1</a></sup> Research in <em>Journal of Dermatological Treatment</em> showed that LI11 stimulation reduced eczema severity and itch intensity.<sup><a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/28767138/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">2</a></sup></p>
    <p class="mb-3">A 2021 study in <em>Inflammation Research</em> demonstrated that LI11 acupressure reduced inflammatory cytokine levels (IL-6, TNF-alpha) in patients with chronic inflammation.<sup><a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/33512508/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">3</a></sup></p>

    </section><section class="mb-8"><h2 class="mb-4">Precautions</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-3 space-y-1 text-stone-700 dark:text-stone-300">
      <li>Avoid if you have a recent elbow injury, fracture, or surgery.</li>
      <li>Do not apply pressure over skin lesions, burns, or rashes at the elbow.</li>
      <li>Use gentle pressure on the elderly or those with fragile skin around the elbow.</li>
      <li>Stop if pressure causes numbness or tingling radiating down the forearm.</li>
    </ul>

    </section><section class="mb-8"><h2 class="mb-4">Related Points</h2>
    <p class="mb-3">LI11 pairs well with <a href="/points/li4-hegu-acupressure-point">LI4 (Hegu)</a> for immune support and allergy relief. For skin conditions, combine with <a href="/points/sp6-sanyinjiao-acupressure-point">SP6 (Sanyinjiao)</a> to cool blood and clear heat.</p>
  </section></article>
